"55,0": {
"v": "\nSPRI clean-up protocol:\n\n*allow beads to sit in RT for 30 mins prior. Ensure you have enough 80% ethanol (500ul per sample).\n\n1. Add room temperature beads to rxn. Mix well by pipetting up and down 10 times.\n2. Incubate for 5 mins at room temperature.\n3. Place samples on magnetic rack, and incubate for 5 mins on the rack.\n4. Remove supernatant and add 200uL of 80% EtOH to samples while on the magnetic rack. \n5. Incubate at room temperature for 30s and remove the supernatant.\n6. Repeat EtOH wash step for a total of 2 times.\n7. Air dry the beads for up to 3-5 mins while on the magnetic rack. Watch beads carefully throughout this incubation to avoid overdrying; smaller bead pellets dry faster. Trust your eyes more than the timer.\n8. Remove tube from magnetic rack. Elute DNA from beads into nuclease free water (can also use 0.1x TE Buffer, 10mM Tris-HCl)\n9. Pipette mix and incubate for a minimum of 5 mins at room temperature off the magnetic rack.\n10. Place on magnetic rack until solution is clear, ~ 5 mins.\n11. Aspirate supernatant and transfer to a clean nuclease free PCR tube.                     \n\n**Checkpoint: Samples can be stored frozen at -20\u00b0C and library prep resumed the next day.\n"
},
"56,0": {
"v": "6. QC of individual libraries",
"bold": true
},
"57,0": {
"v": "Qubit dsDNA HS: ng/ul concentration* of each sample\n\nTapestation, Genomic DNA: nM concentration* and size distribution of each sample\n\nNanodrop dsDNA (optional): identify potential contaminants that may affect pore health\n\n* If individual libraries are too low concentration at this stage, consider moving to step 5.5. Secondary Amplification"
},
"58,0": {
"v": "7. Pooling",
"bold": true
},
"59,0": {
"v": "\nPool all barcoded libraries in the desired ratios to a total of 100-150 fmol in 11 \u00b5L of water (~10-15nM) or elution buffer (EB). See Pooling Calculation Worksheet and NEB calculator: https://nebiocalculator.neb.com/#!/dsdnaamt\n\nComplete QC (Qubit) of pooled libraries.\nPool can be stored at -20C at this stage."
},
"60,0": {
"v": "8. Adapter Ligation + Sequencer Loading",
"bold": true
},
"61,0": {
"v": "Proceed to this step when ready to load the sequencer; see next sheet"
}
},
